    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6a686ff6_201cafa0",
        "filename": "chip/stm32/usb_hid.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 50,
      "author": {
        "id": 1129199
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-07-26T22:19:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why do you need to use BL_SIZE\u003d1 here?\n\nPresumably rx_len should be short enough, right? (and you can\u0027t guarantee it\u0027ll be a multiple of 32 bytes?)",
      "revId": "eb457927547d906f09176a910ced6f3536d8e292",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6aff84b0_faa2f2a0",
        "filename": "chip/stm32/usb_hid.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 50,
      "author": {
        "id": 1116939
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-08-03T08:26:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The rx_len depends on the user of usb_hid.c, they could be sending output report that requires more bytes, so use BL_SIZE\u003d1 is more flexible. Also this allocate the Tx buffer size but the received data size doesn\u0027t to be multiple of 32.",
      "parentUuid": "6a686ff6_201cafa0",
      "revId": "eb457927547d906f09176a910ced6f3536d8e292",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4bf1939b_0a8be2d2",
        "filename": "chip/stm32/usb_hid.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 50,
      "author": {
        "id": 1129199
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-08-09T07:11:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No, the tx buffer size still has a be a multiple of 32, otherwise you may overflow hid_ep_rx_buf if more data than expected is received.\n\nAlso, the value should probably be (((rx_len / 32)-1) \u003c\u003c 10), otherwise you allocate 64 bytes for rx_len\u003d32.\n\nTBH, I\u0027d just set BL_SIZE\u003d0 and worry about it later if we ever want to use \u003e62 bytes transfers.",
      "parentUuid": "6aff84b0_faa2f2a0",
      "revId": "eb457927547d906f09176a910ced6f3536d8e292",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
